From: MyOS <myos@localhost>
Subject: glr2.cc: keep lookahead state in sync when restoring a stack

yyundeleteLastStack() restores an entry in yystates but leaves the parallel
yylookaheadNeeds vector empty.  A later yyremoveDeletes() then accesses the
missing element.  Recent libc++ exposes this as an illegal-instruction trap in
the vector<bool> implementation.

--- a/data/skeletons/glr2.cc
+++ b/data/skeletons/glr2.cc
@@ -1098,6 +1098,7 @@ namespace
       if (yylastDeleted == YY_NULLPTR || !yystates.empty ())
         return;
       yystates.push_back (yylastDeleted);
+      yylookaheadNeeds.push_back (false);
       YYCDEBUG << "Restoring last deleted stack as stack #0.\n";
       clearLastDeleted ();
     }
